<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.3.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01610</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>50b76efc-d8f6-4ed4-b2fd-3e175316c62f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson. Double click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge.</para>

<para>For questions 1 - 2, find the quotients using division.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> \(\frac{45x^5y^9}{-60x^8y^6}\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(-\frac{3x^3}{4y^3}\) </item>
  <item> \(-\frac{4y^3}{3x^3}\) </item>
  <item>\(-\frac{3y^3}{4x^3}\) </item>
  <item>\(-\frac{3}{4}x^3y^3\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>\(-\frac{3y^3}{4x^3}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((48y-24x) \div (2y-x)\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(24\) </item>
  <item> \(-24x\) </item>
  <item> \(24y\) </item>
  <item> \(-24\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(24\)</para>
<para>For questions 3 and 4, divide using long division.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((m^3+1000) \div (m+10)\) </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(m^2+10m\) </item>
  <item>\(
    m^2-100\) </item>
  <item> \(m^2+10m-100\) </item>
  <item> \(m^2-10m+100\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>\(m^2-10m+100\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> \((125y^3-64) \div (5y+4)\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(25y^2-20y+16- \frac{128}{5y+4}\) </item>
  <item> \(25y^2-20y+16- \frac{64}{5y+4}\) </item>
  <item>\(25y^2+20y+16\) </item>
  <item> \(25y^2-20y+16\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(25y^2-20y+16- \frac{128}{5y+4}\)</para>
<para>For questions 5 - 6, divide using synthetic division.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((b^3-3b^2-4b+12) \div (b+2)\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(b^2+5b\); remainder \(6\) </item>
  <item>\( b^2-5b+6\); remainder \(0\) </item>
  <item> \(b^2-5b\); remainder \(6\) </item>
  <item> \(b^2+5b-6\); remainder \(0\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(
  b^2-5b+6\); remainder \(0\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((3x^4-11x^3+2x^2+10x+6) \div (x-3)\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(3x^3+2x^2+4x+2\); remainder \(0\) </item>
  <item> \(3x^3-20x^2-62x-180\); remainder \(0\) </item>
  <item>\(3x^3-2x^2-4x-2\); remainder \(0\) </item>
  <item> \(3x^3-2x^2-4x\); remainder \(–2\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>\(3x^3-2x^2-4x-2\); remainder \(0\)</para>
<para>For questions 7 and 8, use the following polynomial functions.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list>
    <item>\(f(x)=x^2-13x+36\)
    </item>
    <item>\(g(x)=x-4\)</item>
  </list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find \((\frac{f}{g})(x)\).</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x+9\) </item>
  <item> \(x-12\) </item>
  <item> \(x-3\) </item>
  <item> \(x-9\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(x-9\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find \((\frac{f}{g})(-1)\).</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(-8\) </item>
  <item>\( -10\) </item>
  <item>\( -4\) </item>
  <item>\( 8\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>\(-10\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use the Remainder Theorem to find the remainder.</item>
</list>
<para>\(f(x)=x^2-4x-9\) is divided by \(x + 2\)</para>
<list>
  <item>\(3\) </item>
  <item> \(21\) </item>
  <item> \(-13\) </item>
  <item> \(-9\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>\(3\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use the Factor Theorem to determine if \(x-3\) is a factor of \(x^3-7x^2+11x+3\).</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>Yes </item>
  <item>No </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>Yes</para>
</section>
</content>
